[size=6][b]✦ Fairer Magic and Weapon Experience Gains for Sane People[/b][/size]

A friendly adjustment of the way Magic and Weapon experience gains work. Doesnt aim to be an overhaul, but rather to simply illiminate some points of contention and unfairness, as well as reduce the dark-side pull of a common ways of exploiting the morrowind xp system for "effecient" skill leveling (quick attack spam, cheap "practice" spells). At the same time it's not an anti-cheese mod, previously "efficient" tactics are either slightly less efficient or as eficcient as before, BUT this mod makes normal skill use in combat more appealing and effective as a means of natural experience gain. The changes are quite succinct and are listed below:

[list]
[*][b]Magic XP scales with spell cost.[/b] Casting a spell that costs 15 or less magica grants 1x XP, while a spell costing 75 or more magica grants 5x XP.
[*][b]Slow weapons grant more XP per hit, fast ones less.[/b] A dagger hit teaches about 0.6x, a long sword 1.15x, a two-handed axe 1.3x, a bow 1.9x. The exact multiplier depends on a true weapon speed, which is different from the speed displayed in the game since different weapons have different actual speed at 1.0 speed value due to differences in their animation durations.
[*][b]Miscasts and misses still bring a little XP[/b] You do learn from your failures! Only 1/3 of xp that you would've gotten otherwise and, additionally this exp can not actually level up the skill, you still need to succeed atleast once to get over the level up threshold.
[*][b]Conjuration XP from bound gear and Alteration XP from shields[/b], being hit while under an Alteration shield or actively using a Conjured equipment - grants extra XP of the appropriate magic school.
[/list]

Adjustible in setting: Options -> Scripts -> Fairer Magic and Weapon XP.

