[size=5][b]✦ How to install[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Requires OpenMW 0.51 or newer.[/b]
[*]Install and enable [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services (MSS)[/url], it's a required dependency.
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive (or this repository as an archive) and drag and drop it into your mod organiser of choice (e.g [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b] [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy).
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]FairerMagicAndWeaponXP.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher, after [font=Courier New]MaxYariScriptServices.omwscripts[/font].
[/list]

Safe to add to or remove from a game in progress.

[size=5][b]✦ Mod compatibility[/b][/size]

Don't combine it with other mods that scale magic or weapon experience (MBSP, Skill Uses Scaled, NCGDMW's magicka-based progression) - both would scale the same experience. Skill uncappers and level-up overhauls are fine.

Modders: how it works, and its interface, is in the [url=https://github.com/MaxYari/FairerWeaponAndMagicExpGainsOpenMW/blob/main/Sources/DEVELOPMENT.md]technical notes[/url].

[size=5][b]✦ AI disclaimer[/b][/size]

This mod is 95% AI slop, this kind of minor rebalance sounded like a great idea to me, especially in a context of my current playthough and I was not satisfied with the existing solutions (they are either too overloaded or just dont do what this mod does). I also had a paid slopmachine subscription at the time, so slopping this out was fairly straightforward. I am still using this in my playthrough and am quite satisfied with how sublte yet fair the changes are, so I think the mod deserved a right to not just be considered a mere slop. Cheers!
